   "reason": "Same trade on any line: the shield converts a defended blocker into a takeable one, and queen form means the capture square is also the square that threatens the king. | Since the 2026-09-06 rework a converted piece is a CONTROLLED summon, so Sacrifice may detonate it. Steal a guard standing inside the court (unlimited range, free) and blow it up where it stands: the blast is the stolen piece's own attack set (a pawn's two forward diagonals, a knight's eight squares, a queen's rays) plus the ring at T3+, and every capture in the blast stuns the king. Was listed as ILLEGAL before the rework (sacrificeTargets only read controlled summons and a converted piece was an AI ally). Detonation is not gated by the daze (Sacrifice targets the body, it does not move it), so steal-then-blow-up stays a same-turn play.",
